    <string name="forge_token_never_log">The token is stored on device and is never written to logs.</string>
    <string name="forge_token_guide_title">Create and connect a GitHub token</string>
    <string name="forge_token_why">GitHub search stays at about 30 lookups a minute even with a token. DevPulse waits and finishes every app. A token still helps release checks (about 5,000 an hour).</string>
    <string name="forge_token_step_1">1. Open GitHub in a browser and sign in. The GitHub Android app cannot create tokens — it does not make this easier.</string>
    <string name="forge_token_step_2">2. Open Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → Fine-grained tokens.</string>
    <string name="forge_token_step_3">3. Generate a token named DevPulse. Repository access: Public repositories. Leave permissions at the defaults (Metadata: Read).</string>
    <string name="forge_token_step_4">4. Copy the token. GitHub shows it only once.</string>
    <string name="forge_token_step_5">5. Paste it below and tap Save and check. DevPulse asks GitHub if the token works, then stores it encrypted.</string>
    <string name="forge_token_open_step">Open this page</string>
    <string name="forge_token_classic_note">A classic token with no extra boxes checked also works.</string>
